        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am aware of this and it doesn't affect usability until Neovim 1.0 (which is *very* much not near).\nAs it affects not only 'mini.icons', but all 'mini.nvim' modules (as they all use `vim.validate` to check config values), there was a plan to move from `vim.validate` to custom validate helper *in all modules at once*. This will be less lines than having to do it in backward compatible way and should be more robust long term.\n\nI'll take a look at it. Initially it was a plan to do after Neovim 0.11 release, but maybe now (before 'mini.nvim' 0.15.0 release) is a better idea.",
